DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(((ln(x)))^(1/2))+7");
$fun_1 = Formula("(sin(x))^2+4*(8/(x))+3");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-4, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, 6}) U {-4, 6}");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-4, 6} U {-7, 6}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-6, 0} U (-infinity, 13)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(-infinity, 13) U (-infinity, 13) U (-infinity, 13)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`8*6+16`]? [_____]{Real(64.)}
---

What is the value of [`12*19+4/2`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(230.),width=>1}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, 0\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 8\}`]
- [`B = \{-4, 6\}`]
- [`C = \{-7, 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, -2, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -6, 5, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 8, 8, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, -2, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-9, -2, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 5, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 5, -8>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, 5, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, -2, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, 3, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, -6, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, -9, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, 3, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, -6, -10>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 3, 1>") x Compute("<-2, -6, -10>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -6, -10>") x Compute("<-3, -9, 10>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
